{{Quote|They're supposed to be great warriors. Clever, resourceful, proud. Intensely loyal to one another, too.|Eli Vanto, on the Chiss|<ref name="Thrawn" />}}
The '''Chiss''' were a [[near-human]] [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] that possessed [[Color|blue]] skin, red [[eye]]s, and dark blue [[hair]]. They hailed from the [[planet]] [[Csilla]]. The Chiss were notable for the nature and structure of [[Chiss family|their families]], and how Chiss families dominated many aspects of Chiss society.

The [[Chiss Ascendancy]] was located in the [[Unknown Regions]] and had little contact with the rest of [[the galaxy]], and until [[Grand Admiral]] [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo|Thrawn's]] ascent in the ranks of the [[Galactic Empire]], their existence was regarded as mostly a legend even within the Unknown Regions.

==Biology and appearance==
{{Quote|What is he, some kind of Pantoran with an eye condition?|[[Driller MarDapp]], commenting on Thrawn's appearance|<ref name="Thrawn" />}}
[[File:Aralani-Thrawn6.png|thumb|left|180px|The Chiss had blue skin and red eyes.]]
Intimidating beings,<ref name="ThrawnMasterwork">{{Topps|set=2018 Topps Star Wars Masterwork|cardname=Grand Admiral Thrawn}}</ref> Chiss were [[near-human]]s, meaning their [[Humanoid|shape]], features, and dimensions were greatly similar to those of [[human]]s. However, some notable differences<ref name="Thrawn" /> were that their skin was [[Color|blue]], their [[hair]] a shimmering blue-black, their [[eye]]s a glowing red, and they had angular faces.<ref name="ThrawnMasterwork" /> Because of those first two characteristics, they were mistaken for [[Pantoran]]s,<ref name="Thrawn" /> blue-skinned humanoids from [[Pantora]],<ref name="DB Pantoran">{{Databank|pantoran|Pantoran}}</ref> although Pantorans did not have red eyes. Besides their coloration, Chiss eyes were slightly better than those of humans, their visible spectrum going into the [[infrared]] range. Additionally, their hearing was sharper and their reflexes were faster.<ref name="Thrawn" />

[[Force-sensitive|Force-sensitivity]], referred to as the [[The Force|Sight]] by the Chiss, was incredibly rare and manifested in limited abilities, namely [[precognition]], which was ''Third Sight'', and [[telepathy]], which was known as ''Second Sight''. Force-sensitive Chiss were almost always [[Gender|female]]. As they grew older, their abilities diminished and eventually disappeared.<ref name="Thrawn: Alliances">''[[Thrawn: Alliances]]''</ref> The secrets of Second and Third Sights were among the best-kept secrets in the Chiss Ascendancy, to such an extent that many Chiss were unaware of their full extent or even their existence. While he was familiar with the intricacies of Third Sight, Chiss [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[Grand Admiral]] [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo]] knew of the existence of Second Sight but was unaware of its abilities.<ref name="Thrawn Treason" /> Girls identified with the ability to use the Sight were trained to act as [[navigator]]s for the [[Chiss Expansionary Defense Fleet|Chiss fleet]] through the treacherous hyperspace routes of the [[Unknown Regions]]. They were known as ''[[Sky-walker|ozyly-esehembo]]'', the [[Cheunh]] word for "sky-walker."<ref name="Thrawn: Alliances" />

==Society and culture==
{{Quote|One fact has always remained constant: The Chiss must be approached from a position of strength and respect. One must have strength, for the Chiss will deal only with those capable of keeping their promises. One must have respect, for the Chiss must believe that those promises ''will'' be kept.|Passage from [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo's journal]]|<ref name="Thrawn" />}}
[[File:ChissSpyMask-CaM.png|thumb|200px|A Chiss spy impersonating an Imperial officer removes her face mask.]]
The ruling class of the [[Chiss Ascendancy]] was known as the [[Aristocra (organization)|Aristocra]]. The supreme legislative and executive body of the Ascendancy was the [[Chiss Syndicure]]. The [[Ascendancy military|Chiss military]] consisted of the [[Chiss Defense Force]] and the [[Chiss Expansionary Defense Fleet]].<ref name="Chaos Rising" />

The Chiss were renowned throughout the Unknown Regions for their military might as well as their perceived just [[Non-intervention policy|military doctrine]]. Even among species with no direct contact with the Chiss Ascendancy, stories and legends of the Chiss as blue-skinned noble warriors flourished. This was true even among species that had apparently performed no space travel for [[Standard decade|decades]]. During a [[Sunrise's civil war|devastating civil war]] on [[Sunrise|her homeworld]], a leader named [[the Magys]] fled with 200 [[refugee]]s to the [[Rapacc system]], where they [[Unidentified city (Rapacc)|settled]]. The Magys' refugees warned the native [[Paccosh]] of [[Agbui|invaders]] who would seek to destroy the Paccosh people, and encouraged them to dispatch refugees to preserve their culture. She told her hosts legends of the Chiss as noble warriors famously capable of disabling their enemies without destroying them, leading the Paccosh to send a refugee ship to the [[Dioya system]] at the edge of Chiss space in the hopes of seeking Chiss aid. [[Uingali foar Marocsaa]] later tested the identity of Senior Captain Thrawn by challenging him to disable a Paccosh freighter without destroying it.<ref name="Greater Good" />

The primary Chiss [[language]] was [[Cheunh]],<ref name="Thrawn Treason" /> though in their rare contacts with outsiders, the Chiss used [[trade language]]s such as [[Sy Bisti]], [[Meese Caulf]], [[Taarja]], and [[Minnisiat]].<ref name="Thrawn" /><ref name="Chaos Rising" /> [[Writing|Written]] communication was done in the [[Cheunh script]].<ref name="Thrawn Treason" /> Those who disliked Chiss used the derogatory nickname "blueskin" for them.<ref name="Chaos Rising" />

Most Chiss names were multisyllabic and consisted of three parts, as in Mitth'raw'nuruodo. The first portion identified an individual's [[Chiss family|family]], the second was the given name, and the third indicated other social factors.<ref name="Thrawn Treason" /> Aside from the long form of their names, the Chiss also used shortened variants&mdash;for example, "Mit'''th'raw'n'''uruodo" could be shortened to "Thrawn."<ref name="Thrawn" /> These short form names were known as [[core name]]s, and for the sake of expediency, core names were conventionally used in all except the most formal situations. In a rare case of an outsider among the Chiss, the human [[Eli N. Vanto|Eli Vanto]] was given the standard three-part name "Eli'van'to," which his shipmates reduced to the core name "Ivant."<ref name="Thrawn Treason" />

Chiss were [[Diet|omnivorous]] and ate foods such as [[Unidentified cheese|cheese]], [[yubal]], and plant products.<ref name="Greater Good" />

==History==
{{Quote|Because I know these Chiss, Generalirius. They are resilient and powerful. I've seen them resist attack from without and manipulation from within. Only a combination of the two will succeed in bringing about their destruction|"[[Jixtus]]" to [[Generalirius]] [[Nakirre]]|<ref name="Lesser Evil">''[[Thrawn Ascendancy: Lesser Evil]]''</ref>}}
[[File:Thrawn-TGTB.png|thumb|left|270px|Grand Admiral Thrawn, a notable Chiss.]]
The Chiss hailed from [[Csilla]], a planet located in the so-called Unknown Regions of [[the galaxy]]. The Chiss and other inhabitants of the [[Unknown Regions]] called them "The Chaos," referring to the hazardous nature of [[Navigator|navigation]] within the region. Millennia earlier, the Chiss had contact with the greater galaxy, and were politically and militarily drawn into [[Sith Wars|the ancient wars]] between the Galactic Republic and the [[Sith Empire]], but eventually broke off contact with both entities and withdrew back into the Unknown Regions, sealing their borders. During the [[Republic Era]]<ref name="Chaos Rising" /> and [[Imperial Era]],<ref name="Thrawn" /> they were ruled by a government known as the [[Chiss Ascendancy]]. According to [[Generalirius]] [[Nakirre]] of the [[Kilji Illumine]], the [[Kilji way of order and enlightenment]] could make the Chiss and the Ascendancy work for the glory of the Grysks&mdash;indirectly serving the Kiljis.<ref name="Lesser Evil" /> The [[Outer Rim Territories]] [[planet]] [[Serenno]] was home to some Chiss.<ref name="BMF70">{{BuildFalconCite|70|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref>

Despite their secrecy, one Chiss known as Mitth'raw'nuruodo became an [[Imperial officer|officer]] of the Galactic Empire. Attaining the [[Military rank|rank]] of Grand Admiral,<ref name="Thrawn" /> he participated in the [[Imperial Military]]'s efforts to [[Early rebellion against the Galactic Empire|combat the early rebellion]] in the [[Standard year|years]] prior to the [[Battle of Yavin]].<ref name="Steps Into Shadow">''[[Star Wars Rebels: Steps Into Shadow]]''</ref> Shortly after the [[Battle of Yavin|Battle]] of [[Yavin 4|Yavin]], former [[Senator]] [[Johhar Kessen]] acquired the services of several female Chiss [[Mercenary|mercenaries]].<ref name="Commander">''[[Star Wars: Commander]]''</ref> During the [[Galactic Civil War]], a female Chiss [[spy]] infiltrated the Empire posing as a human Imperial officer using [[Synthskin|fake skin]].<ref name="Cyphers and Masks">''[[Cyphers and Masks]]''</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Kallus_Chiss.png|thumb|right|250px|An early design of Alexsandr Kallus depicted him as a Chiss.]]
The Chiss species first appeared, albeit unidentified, in ''[[Heir to the Empire]]'', a [[1991]] [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] novel written by [[Timothy Zahn]] as the first entry in [[Star Wars: The Thrawn Trilogy|''The Thrawn Trilogy'']].<ref name="Heir to the Empire">''[[Heir to the Empire]]''</ref> The species' name would later be revealed in ''[[Vision of the Future]]'', a [[1998]] Legends novel also written by Zahn as the second entry in ''[[Star Wars: The Hand of Thrawn Duology]]''.<ref name="Vision of the Future">''[[Vision of the Future]]''</ref> The Chiss became [[canon]] when they appeared in ''Secret Alliances'', the sixth campaign featured in ''[[Star Wars: Commander]]'', a mobile game published by [[Disney Interactive]]<ref name="Commander" /> that was released on [[August 21]], [[2014]].<ref name="Star Wars: Commander release date">{{Tumblr|subdomain=disneyinteractive|url=post/97146518477/star-wars-commander-plans-have-been-intercepted|name=Disney Interactive|text="Star Wars: Commander" Plans Have Been Intercepted Detailing Who is Winning the Galactic Civil War|quote=Five million players have now joined the war (downloaded Star Wars: Commander since its launch on August 21).|archivefile=File:Disney_Interactive_Commander_release_date.png}}</ref>

Though he was ultimately made a [[human]], a preliminary design of [[Agent]] [[Alexsandr Kallus|Kallus]], one of the antagonists of the canon animated television series ''[[Star Wars Rebels]]'', depicted him as a Chiss.<ref name="Meet Kallus">{{SWYouTube|7zstnZrz_3M|Meet Agent Kallus, Imperial Enforcer &#124; Star Wars Rebels|sw_url=video/star-wars-rebels-meet-agent-kallus-imperial-enforcer}}</ref> Eventually, the Chiss appeared in the series, in the form of Grand Admiral Thrawn.<ref name="Thrawn" /> During development of the ''[[Star Wars: The High Republic]]'' multimedia project, illustration manager [[Jeffrey Thomas]] wanted [[Marchion Ro]] to be a Chiss out of admiration for Thrawn, but his idea didn't pan out<ref name="Art of THR">''[[The Art of Star Wars: The High Republic: Volume I]]''</ref> and of Ro's species was eventually canonized as [[Evereni]] in the [[2022]] [[Star Wars comic books|comic]] [[The High Republic: Eye of the Storm 1|''The High Republic: Eye of the Storm'' 1]].<ref name="Eye of the Storm 1">[[The High Republic: Eye of the Storm 1|''The High Republic: Eye of the Storm'' 1]]</ref>

